<title>BRAZIL: BRAZIL SENATE TO VOTE ON NEW CENBANK HEAD TUESDAY.</title>
<headline>BRAZIL SENATE TO VOTE ON NEW CENBANK HEAD TUESDAY.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The full floor of the Brazilian Senate will vote on the nomination of Gustavo Franco as the new Central Bank president next Tuesday, said Senator Jose Roberto Arruda, government leader in Congress.</p>
<p>The Senate's Economic Affairs Committee Thursday approved the nomination of Franco, currently director of international affairs, who has been nominated to replace outgoing Central Bank President Gustavo Loyola.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-3141193))</p>
